{
  "_comment": "Materials, weapons, armour and bodies for the colony's blows (Dwarf Fortress's items: the attack's geometry on the item, the physics on the material). density g/cm3 (a weapon's mass is its head of the material plus its haft of wood); hard = shear yield, relative: an edge bites a layer only when its material is at least 'bite' x as hard, else the blow turns blunt there, and the harder the edge against the layer the less it pays ((layer/edge)^'hardness'); edge = how keen an edge it takes (0-1); resist = the cost per mm for an edge to cut it; absorb = what each mm takes from a blunt blow; fracture = what each mm of a rigid layer (plate, bone) takes to crack; rigid layers ring and turn blows. Flags are DF's capability flags: weapon, armour. A blow's momentum is 'momentum' x strength x velocity x sqrt(kg); a beast's is its weapon's force x size^'size_power'. An edge stopped at the bone cracks it with what is left past 'crack' x its fracture; a blow spread by armour needs 'spread' x. An edge stopped in the muscle past 'deep' of it has bitten deep. A blow's harm is 'harm' x the share of the part's resistance it went through ('blunt' x that for a blunt blow; bone counts 'bone_share' of its cost to an edge).",
  "momentum": 100,
  "harm": 1.75,
